This product includes software developed for running AlmaLinux on Cisco ENCS
5400 series appliances with the built-in Marvell switch operational.

------------------------------------------------------------------------------
PRIOR ART
------------------------------------------------------------------------------

The core discovery that the Marvell BobCat2 switch in an ENCS 5400 can be
bootstrapped from a PCI-passthrough VM is the work of yeyus:

    Switch bootstrap VM
    https://yeyus.notion.site/Switch-bootstrap-VM-04cac1d64bde48b684c51e8dac524245
    https://forums.servethehome.com/index.php?members/yeyus.35233/

That write-up identified the Marvell PCI device (11ab:be00), the out-of-tree
mv_pciboot kernel module and remote-bootd loader inside Cisco's switch-confd
package, the SMBIOS product-name gate a VM must satisfy, and the requirement to
pin the kernel to the version the module was built against.

This repository automates that process and adds switch management tooling.

Hardware analysis of the ENCS 5412 — NIC layout, internal switch topology, and
the observation that NFVIS releases after 4.15.x disable the switch — came from
the ServeTheHome community thread:

    https://forums.servethehome.com/index.php?threads/127-cisco-encs5412-k9-xeon-d-1557-12-core-32g-ram.42638/

